_at":"2025-05-06T13:50:51Z"},"body":"#91006 introduced a minor regression with how errors are printed for the case where there are no script backtraces, where they now add empty lines after the `at:` part, one for every registered script language:\r\n\r\n```\r\nERROR: Expected Image data size of 256x256x1 (DXT5 RGBA8 with 8 mipmaps) = 87408 bytes, got 87360 bytes instead.\r\n   at: initialize_data (./core/io/image.cpp:2230)\r\n\r\nERROR: Invalid image: image is empty\r\n   at: create_from_image (./scene/resources/image_texture.cpp:77)\r\n\r\nERROR: Failed loading resource: res://broken.dds. Make sure resources have been imported by opening the project in the editor at least once.\r\n   at: _load (./core/io/resource_loader.cpp:342)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes that by checking whether the backtraces are empty before printing them, in all the relevant places.\r\n\r\nNote that this could also be fixed in a less intrusive way, by simply changing `Engine.capture_script_backtraces` to not include empty backtraces at all, but I'm personally of the opinion that a backtrace should always be returned for every registered script language, to clearly indicate that there are indeed no stack frames for that particular script language.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.githu